In article <42202@bbn.COM>, lkaplan@bbn.com (Larry Kaplan) writes:
> Conquer version 4.0 seems to have problems when it runs out of nations slots.
> The previously mentioned newlogin() problem is one manifestation.
> If you use the entire npc nations file, you are only left with one free
> nation.  This means that you can only add one more and if a revolt occurs
> it really corrupts the system by trying to create a new nation.  I haven't
> looked into the cause but have just commented out a bunch of the npcs.

The fix here is to turn up the definition of NTOTAL in the headers files.
I set mine to 35 and the problem goes away.  There are already 24 NPC nations
by default so after you add your first new nation it runs out of space.


